==Boss slayer==
Players who have [[Slayer Rewards#Unlock|unlocked]] the ''Like a boss'' ability via spending 200 [[Slayer reward points]] can be assigned bosses by [[Konar quo Maten|Konar]], [[Nieve]]/[[Steve]], [[Duradel]]/[[Kuradal]], or [[Krystilia]]. The [[Slayer master]] will randomly assign a boss for which the player meets the below requirements. This allows players to benefit from a black mask or slayer helmet (including imbued), making boss slayer more lucrative. However, players will not be eligible for most speed-based [[Combat Achievements]] (even if they aren't using either one) and they have no effect on the awakened versions of the post-quest Desert Treasure II bosses.

Boss slayer will not account for any blocked or toggled off tasks, as it is a separate task compared to general monsters. For example, players can still be assigned [[Kree'arra]] even if they do not have [[aviansie]]s toggled on, as long as they have access to God Wars Dungeon. Substitutes are accepted for a few boss tasks, if they have one; if assigned a [[Vet'ion]] task, players may alternatively kill [[Calvar'ion]] in his place. 

Konar is a unique exception to boss assignments; while the [[deranged archaeologist]] is an acceptable substitute for the [[crazy archaeologist]], this does not apply to her tasks. She can also assign Wilderness bosses even though her general tasks will never send players there. She can also assign [[Araxxor]] despite not offering [[araxyte]]s and is the only one who can assign the [[Alchemical Hydra]] boss task.

[[Krystilia]] will only roll boss tasks in the Wilderness, barring the [[King Black Dragon]] as his lair is not considered part of it.

After determining the boss, the Slayer Master will ask the player to select the amount that they want to kill for their assignment. The player can select anywhere from 3–35 kills (36 if [[Barrows]] is assigned). The maximum assignment can be increased by completing [[Combat Achievement]] tiers, with each tier adding +5 to the cap, up to 65 at Grandmaster tier.

If the player is assigned a boss task but cancels out of the dialogue, the Slayer master will remind the player of it before asking how much they would like to kill. 

Upon finishing a boss task, the player will get an additional 5,000 Slayer experience regardless of task length. If the effect of a [[slayer cape]] activates for a boss task, it is possible for the player to be assigned a different boss.

If players do not wish to kill the boss they have been assigned, they can pay 30 [[Slayer reward point|Slayer reward points]] to skip the task as with regular tasks. However, this is not generally recommended, as many consider the 30 Slayer point cost to be high, and higher level players can usually complete the task quickly by assigning 3 kills. The only way to "block" a boss is by toggling the ability off, though this '''does not''' refund points, and the 200 point cost must be paid again to toggle it back on.

[[Duradel]]/[[Kuradal]] has a [[Slayer task#Task weighing|task weighting]] of 12 for boss Slayer tasks, whereas [[Konar quo Maten|Konar]], [[Nieve]]/[[Steve]], and [[Krystilia]] each have a task weighting of 8.

Slayer masters '''cannot''' assign the following as bosses:

*[[Corporeal Beast]]
*[[Hespori]]
*[[Skotizo]] (although killable as a [[Black Demon]] or [[Greater Demon]] task)
*[[Obor]] (killable as a [[Slayer task/Hill giants|hill giant]] task)
*[[Bryophyta]] (although killable as a [[Slayer task/Moss giants|moss giant]] task)
*[[The Mimic]]
*[[The Nightmare]] (and [[Phosani's Nightmare|Phosani variant]])
*[[Nex]]
*[[Scurrius]] (although killable as part of a [[Slayer task/Rats|rats]] task)
*[[Perilous Moons]]
*[[The Hueycoatl]]
*[[Amoxliatl]] (although killable as part of a [[Slayer task/Lesser Nagua|lesser nagua]] task)
*[[Royal Titans]] (although killable as part of a [[Slayer task/Ice giants|ice giant]] or [[Slayer task/Fire giants|fire giant]] task for [[Eldric the Ice King]] and [[Branda the Fire Queen]] respectively)
*[[Yama]]
*[[Doom of Mokhaiotl]]
*All raid bosses (aside from [[Lizardman shaman (Chambers of Xeric)|lizardman shamans]] on a [[Lizardman]] task or [[Skeletal Mystic|skeletal mystics]] on a [[skeleton]] task in the [[Chambers of Xeric]])

